*Identification metric/naming:*

From data protection POV:

* as for the Fleets, I do not see a problem here - we just must make sure that we have the right to use any IP (trademarks, etc) if we decide to.
{color:#ff991f}Noted. Naming fleets after their actual names would be preferable. What would this process look like?{color}
* as for the drivers, if we want to ensure the data is pseudonymised (as we agreed prior), we must make sure that only the driver can understand their score on the website (and relevant Bolt employees). Because of this, I ideally I would prefer to replace driver ID with some made up identifier.
{color:#ff991f}Just to understand, is pseudonymised data and ditching the use of driver ID a legal requirement, or just a preference? Given that we will have hundreds of drivers, we want to make it easy for them to identify their scores and avoid the headache of replacing all those driver IDs with fictitious names.{color}

*Opt-out via Google Form*

_Can we communicate a final date they can opt-out via Google Form, i.e. 2 days after receiving the email?_

At least for drivers, they ideally must be able to opt out at any time. Technical difficulties to implement opt out are not a valid reason not to provide opt out options.

{color:#ff991f}Again, is this a legal requirement, or just a preference? I’d just like to avoid the team needing to check this daily and remove any opt-outs as this will be rather time-consuming. as far as I’m aware, we didn’t follow this approach in the previous driver leagues.{color}

{color:#ff991f}Do I understand correctly that for fleets we can communicate an end date for opt-out? E.g “{color}{color:#ff991f}_If you prefer not to have your fleet participate in the Formula Bolt campaign, you can easily opt-out. Click the link below to unsubscribe before June 5 at 9:00 and we'll ensure your fleet is not included in this campaign.”_{color}

Also, opt out to unsubscribe from emails must be available for all emails that driver/fleet are receiving.

{color:#ff991f}Do you mean the regular banner we include in comms with an option to opt-out?{color}

We can definitely avoid opt-out *if* we make the enrolment opt-in based - i.e. if the driver/fleet received the emails and actively chose to participate.

{color:#ff991f}Would like to avoid this as historically drivers/fleets don't engage with our communications, I'm pretty sure this approach would result in very low participation.{color}

If it's technically difficult to provide opt-out, I would advise to make the campaign *opt-in* based.

{color:#ff991f}It's not technically difficult, it's just a very time-consuming task.{color}

