Regarding sessions expiration, i agree with Ioana, it should be considered separately from passkeys.

{quote}For how long do we store it? It does not mean that if the user logs out, we erase the id and passkey, right? We just invalidate the session, but the user can easily logs in back{quote}

We store it indefinitely. This is what enables the user to log in using the passkey they created. This is not sensitive info, it’s just a way of connecting a passkey with a user. Indeed, the user can easily log back in (otherwise passkeys would be pretty useless).

{quote}_and a public key for decoding the sign in requests._{quote}

We store it indefinitely. This is not sensitive info either and we need it in order to decode user authentication requests using a passkey.

